# herocn context

This repo is **herocn**: a Next.js 16 demo + `@herocn` shadcn registry + agent skills that restyle shadcn/ui (Base UI, nova) to a HeroUI v3 look. It is not HeroUI itself and not an npm component package.

**Before doing work, read `PROJECT.md`.** That file is the product spec for new chats. `HANDOFF.md` is a stale work log. `AGENTS.md` is auto-generated by Next.js — follow its Next-docs instruction, not as the product spec.

## Hard rules

- Never invent token or colour values; say NOT FOUND.
- Do not override `components/ui/*` look (radius, border, shadow, colour, padding, focus, motion) from call-site `className`. Layout classes are fine.
- Do not swap Base UI for another primitive library or break props/exports.
- Do not copy heroui.com images, logos, or wallpapers.
- Package manager is **Bun** (`bun.lock`). Consumer CLI examples stay `npx`.
- Conventional Commits only; commit only when asked.
- No nested `<button>`/`<a>`. Verify UI in the browser when behaviour or layout changes.
